This repository distributes the firmware of the "Minuteur M5Dial" kitchen timer in binary form only
(the "Firmware": the signed application images, bootloader, partition table and OTA data files
published in this repository's releases and on its web installer), together with the files used to
publish it. The source code of the Firmware is not published.

1. Grant. Subject to the terms below, you may, free of charge, download the Firmware and install it,
   with the provided web installer, its over-the-air update function or any other means, on M5Stack
   Dial devices that you own or lawfully control, and use it on those devices for your personal,
   non-commercial purposes.

2. Restrictions. Except as expressly permitted by this licence or by applicable law, you may not:
   (a) redistribute, publish, sell, rent, lend or otherwise make the Firmware available to third
       parties, in whole or in part, including by hosting copies of it or by pre-installing it on
       devices you sell or give away; share a link to this repository or to its web installer instead;
   (b) modify, adapt, translate or create derivative works of the Firmware, or remove or alter its
       signature;
   (c) reverse engineer, decompile or disassemble the Firmware, except to the extent that applicable
       law expressly permits it notwithstanding this limitation (in particular for interoperability);
   (d) remove or alter any copyright notice or licence information.

3. Third-party components. The Firmware and the web installer contain components published by third
   parties under their own open-source licences, listed in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md with their full
   texts in the LICENSES directory. Nothing in this licence restricts the rights you have under those
   licences for those components.

4. Ownership. The Firmware is licensed, not sold. All rights not expressly granted are reserved by the
   copyright holder.

5. No warranty. THE FIRMWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED,
   INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE
   AND NON-INFRINGEMENT. Installing firmware on a device carries risks: you do so at your own risk.
   A kitchen timer must not be relied upon where a missed alarm could cause harm.

6. Limitation of liability. TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW, IN NO EVENT SHALL THE
   COPYRIGHT HOLDER BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF
   CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM, OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE FIRMWARE OR ITS USE.

7. Termination. This licence ends automatically if you breach it; you must then delete the Firmware
